{"agent_id":"pp3g-HdGN-audit-read-only-flag-only-independently-verify-the","agent_seq":1,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T07:03:46.278044059Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"cc0b5266-1d21-49d3-b396-20a9a2d10f9e","comment_uuid":"dd259859-22a1-4dd8-8fdc-05f6a38b64ee","author":"pp3g-HdGN-audit-read-only-flag-only-independently-verify-the","content":"**AUDIT VERDICT: CONDITIONAL PASS**\n\nIndependent verification of `docs/research/registry/Failure-Matrix.md` (issue #392 deliverable, commit f1500650). Findings organized by audit scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. ARCHITECTURAL ASSESSMENT\n\n### 1a. Accuracy — Evidence Citations\n\n**[CONCERN] Phantom Issue Citations — #506, #519, #522 do not exist in crosslink.**\n\nThe matrix header (line 31) and Evidence Sources section (lines 98-104) cite three issues as primary evidence:\n- `#506 regression-stall report` — `crosslink issue show 506` returns \"Issue #506 not found\"\n- `#519` (HMS post-mortem) — `crosslink issue show 519` returns \"Issue #519 not found\"\n- `#522 doc-navigation probe` — `crosslink issue show 522` returns \"Issue #522 not found\"\n\nThe HMS post-mortem document itself exists at `to-file/hms-research-session-postmortem-2026-08-17.md` and its content is accurate where cited. But the issue-number attribution cannot be verified through the tracking system. These may be cross-repo references (tripn-astro) — if so, that should be documented.\n\n**[CONCERN] Phantom Document Citation — agent-orchestration-playbook does not exist.**\n\nThe playbook is the single most heavily cited evidence source in the matrix:\n- Line 78: playbook §5.3 (agent infinite loop)\n- Line 79: playbook §5.3 (agent exceeds duration)\n- Line 80: playbook §5.3 (legitimate exceeds)\n- Line 81: playbook §5.3 (worker dies)\n- Line 82: playbook §4 (relaunch)\n- Line 83: playbook §5.8 (engine restarts)\n- Line 86: playbook §2.1 (repeats work)\n- Line 87: playbook §5.4 (partial progress)\n- Line 89: playbook §5.6 (workers collide)\n- Line 90: playbook §5.7 (orchestrator loses context)\n- Line 110: playbook §5.3/§5.4/§5.6/§5.8 (evidence sources)\n\nNo file named `agent-orchestration-playbook.md` exists anywhere in the repository. `crosslink knowledge search \"agent orchestration playbook\"` returns no results. The knowledge cache contains no matching page. This is a verifiability gap — 10 of 13 rows cite a document that cannot be located.\n\n**[OK] HMS Post-Mortem Citations Verified.**\n\nCross-checked against `to-file/hms-research-session-postmortem-2026-08-17.md`:\n- §9 pathological monitoring loops (line 98 citation) → verified at post-mortem lines 92-111\n- §4 unrequested builder dispatch (line 82 citation) → verified at post-mortem lines 40-46\n- §3 theorizing from source code (line 90 citation) → verified at post-mortem lines 32-37\n\n**[OK] Handoff-Failure-Analysis Citation Verified.**\n\nLine 86 citation: \"fresh model instance reconstructed plausible project model while lacking validation mechanisms\" → verified at `docs/research/handoff-failure-analysis.md` line 60. Accurate characterization.\n\n**[CONCERN] Worker Dies — Evidence Mismatch (line 81).**\n\nRow \"Worker dies\" cites: \"Handoff-failure-analysis.md: agent session degraded into generation loop\" as supporting evidence. But the handoff-failure-analysis describes a **generation loop** (agent emitting repeated tokens without progress), not a **process crash/death** (agent process killed or crashed). These are distinct failure modes:\n- Generation loop = liveness failure (agent running but producing no useful work)\n- Worker death = process failure (agent process terminated)\n\nThe generation-loop evidence better supports \"Agent infinite loop\" (which already has its own row). \"Worker dies\" needs evidence of actual process termination — e.g., tmux session killed, OOM, systemd service restart.\n\n**[CONCERN] Multiple Workers Collide — Evidence Mismatch (line 89).**\n\nRow \"Multiple workers collide\" cites: \"Playbook §5.6: reviewer independence via isolated sub-issues; contamination incident documented where second reviewer read first reviewer's verdict.\" This describes **review-contamination** (information leakage between reviewers), not **resource collision** (concurrent modification of shared state). These are different failure classes. The crosslink lock system does prevent resource collision, but the cited evidence doesn't demonstrate that failure mode.\n\n### 1b. Accuracy — Confidence Levels\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Agent exceeds expected duration\" rated Well Established (line 79).**\n\nThe \"Well Established\" level requires \"extensively documented, root causes understood.\" The evidence cited is: HMS post-mortem (one incident) + playbook §5.3 (unverifiable). One post-mortem + one phantom document does not meet the threshold. Recommend downgrading to \"High.\"\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Orchestrator loses context\" rated High (line 90).**\n\nThe \"High\" level requires \"consistent pattern with multiple independent confirmations.\" The evidence cited is: HMS post-mortem §3 (one incident) + playbook §5.7 (unverifiable). Only one confirmed incident. Recommend downgrading to \"Moderate.\"\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Engine restarts\" rated High (line 83).**\n\nEvidence is solely playbook §5.8 — which does not exist locally. Without verifiable evidence, this should be \"Moderate\" at most.\n\n### 1c. Accuracy — Hookability\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Queue item disappears\" rated Partial hookable (line 84).**\n\nRow states: \"Not directly observed in current sessions; identified as architectural requirement.\" If the failure has never been observed and the mitigation (queue mechanics) is not yet implemented, \"Partial\" is generous. Recommend \"No\" until queue mechanics exist and can be tested.\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Timer disappears\" rated Partial hookable (line 85).**\n\nSame issue — no observed evidence, no implemented mitigation. Recommend \"No\" until timer persistence is implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 2. REGISTRY-CONVENTION COMPLIANCE\n\n**[OK] Frontmatter** (lines 1-26). Follows the AI Capability Registry Specification pattern with all expected fields: title, program, layer, document_type, status, authority, canonical_repository, depends_on, consumed_by, related_documents, supersedes, review_frequency, last_reviewed. Compliant.\n\n**[OK] Evidence Quality Framework** (lines 49-58). Matches the Specification's 6-level hierarchy exactly (Spec lines 349-355). Compliant.\n\n**[OK] Confidence Assessment Framework** (lines 62-70). Matches the Specification's 5-level framework exactly (Spec lines 321-328). Compliant.\n\n**[OK] last_reviewed: 2026-08-18** (line 24). Reasonable for initial creation.\n\n**[CONCERN] review_frequency: \"Monthly (or per-session)\"** (line 23). The Specification suggests \"Monthly.\" Adding \"(or per-session)\" is a reasonable operational extension but deviates from the Spec without documenting the rationale. This is minor but should be noted as a deliberate extension.\n\n---\n\n## 3. PRIORITIZATION ASSESSMENT\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Engine restarts\" misplaced in priority tiers.**\n\nMatrix row: Confidence = High, Hookable = Yes. Per the tier definitions (lines 118-119: \"High Priority: High Confidence + Yes Hookable\"), this belongs in High Priority. But it is listed in Medium Priority (line 133).\n\n**[CONCERN] \"Orchestrator loses context\" misplaced in priority tiers.**\n\nMatrix row: Confidence = High, Hookable = Partial. Per the tier definitions (line 129: \"Medium Priority: Moderate Confidence + Yes/Partial Hookable\"), this belongs in Medium Priority. But it is listed in Lower Priority (line 140). (Note: if the confidence is downgraded to Moderate per finding 1b above, it still belongs in Medium Priority, not Lower.)\n\n---\n\n## 4. SYSTEMIC RISKS\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|--------|------------|\n| Phantom document citations (playbook) | 10/13 rows cite unverifiable source; entire evidence base is weakened | Locate, create, or replace playbook references with verified sources |\n| Phantom issue citations (#506/#519/#522) | Primary evidence chain broken; auditability compromised | Verify cross-repo issue IDs or replace with local evidence |\n| Evidence-class mismatches (worker dies, workers collide) | Wrong failure mode diagnosed; hooks may target wrong symptoms | Correct evidence citations to match actual failure classes |\n| Overstated confidence levels | Prioritization may be skewed; hooks may be deployed prematurely | Downgrade confidence to match actual evidence quantity |\n\n---\n\n## 5. PRECONDITIONS FOR FULL PASS\n\n1. **Locate or replace the agent-orchestration-playbook references.** Either the playbook exists in another repo/location and should be cross-referenced, or the 10+ playbook citations should be replaced with verified local sources.\n2. **Verify or correct issue-number attributions.** Confirm #506, #519, #522 exist in tripn-astro or replace with verifiable local references.\n3. **Correct evidence mismatches.** \"Worker dies\" row needs process-crash evidence. \"Multiple workers collide\" row needs concurrent-modification evidence.\n4. **Downgrade confidence levels.** \"Agent exceeds expected duration\" → High. \"Orchestrator loses context\" → Moderate. \"Engine restarts\" → Moderate.\n5. **Fix priority-tier placement.** Move \"Engine restarts\" to High Priority. Move \"Orchestrator loses context\" to Medium Priority.\n6. **Harden hookability for unobserved failures.** \"Queue item disappears\" and \"Timer disappears\" should be \"No\" until their mitigations are implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n## 6. WHAT IS SOUND\n\n- The 13 failure classes are reasonable and well-chosen — they cover the observed failure spectrum from liveness to context to coordination.\n- The Required Semantic column is generally well-written — the preventive/detective semantics are appropriately abstract.\n- The Evidence Quality and Confidence frameworks faithfully reproduce the AI Capability Registry Specification.\n- The Maintenance section (lines 146-159) defines a sensible update protocol.\n- The Relationship to Other Documents section (lines 163-169) correctly situates the matrix within the document ecosystem.\n- The Purpose section (lines 38-45) clearly distinguishes this matrix from the AI Capability Registry.\n\n**Audit posted as observation on #402. Awaiting operator judgment on preconditions.","created_at":"2026-08-18T07:03:46.268806224Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:j2h7ascrf//mwW/he7Ckff+n7+EACv/0qNg0mwgCyww","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgvn0jDBrvA84gkioOk7QkcQCxQH0soLPEa7lnsQuw68cAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAsNoRp6Wsw4MM/WxxeU0JGFgT5wnaQa9ff3C0f26eOkCkE4jMP/i+BCbZV4WuoeX40B1yh0+c/sIfYLcIrhYwCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:j2h7ascrf//mwW/he7Ckff+n7+EACv/0qNg0mwgCyww","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgvn0jDBrvA84gkioOk7QkcQCxQH0soLPEa7lnsQuw68cAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBUec6ilYZERxWmAZP+NrqGx9zzEjTB6UQJ7bHklkDrmG2E/oiI1SZs112+GquyBdyMyzfDGDDTaAaik5svlgQ4="}
